{"id":"word:hebrew:H6435","type":"word","title":"פֵּן","subtitle":"H6435 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, removal ; used only (in the construction) adverb as conjunction, lest","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פֵּן (H6435) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: conj.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 133 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פֵּן (pên) means properly, removal ; used only (in the construction) adverb as conjunction, lest First listed occurrence: 1Chr 10 4."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פֵּן","transliteration":"pên","pronunciation":"pane","strong":"H6435","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6435","partOfSpeech":"conj","forms":["פֶּן","פֶּֽן","פֶּ֚ן","וּ/פֶן","פֶּ֨ן"],"morphs":[["HC",128],["HC/C",5]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, removal ; used only (in the construction) adverb as conjunction, lest","usage":"(lest) (peradventure), that...not.","full":"H6435. pen מֶּןֿ 133 (always with Makkeph **except Gen 38:23 ; 44:34 ; Deut 7:25 ; 32:27 [not Gi], Isa 27:3 ; Prov 25:8 : Mandelkern Conc. under the word .) conjunction (averting, or deprecating), lest (origin dubious: Thes Kö ii. 334 from מָּנָה , properly substantive construct in accusative for the aversion of ; but פָנָה is intransitive: Nö M. 474 compares the enclitic particle מּוֺן in ᵑ7 , then ἄν , 'etwa,' thinking that a particle with the meaning 'es möchte etwa,' spoken in a tone of alarm, might readily acquire a deprecatory force); — lest: 1 with imperfect Gen 3:3 ye shall not eat thereof . . . מֶּןתְּֿמֻתוּן lest ye die, 11:4 let us build a city מֶּןנָֿפוּץ lest we be scattered, 19:15 , 17 , 19 ; 38:23 ; Genesis 45: Exod 1:10 ; 23:29 ; 23:33 etc., 2Kin 10:23 (followed by יֵשׁ ), Isa 6:10 ; 27:3 ; 28:22 ; 48:5 , 7 ; Psa 2:12 ; 7:3 etc.; often after הִשָׁמֶרלְֿךָ take heed to thyself Gen 24:6 ; 31:24 , and especially in Deuteronomy, as Deut 4:9 , 23 ; 6:12 ; 8:11 and elsewhere; after a verb of fearing Gen 32:12 , and once, even, of swearing Judg 15:12 ; deprecating pathetically, Gen 44:34 how shall I go up, etc.? lest I look upon the evil that will befal my father. Once, unusually, preceding the principal clause, Prov 5:6 מֶּןתְּֿפַלֵּס חַיִּים אֹרַח lest she should make level the path of life, her ways are unstable, etc. (Ew Be Now; see also Toy). Note especially a. the idiom מֶּןֿ (אָמַרְתִּי) אָמַר כִּי for he ( I ) said, Lest... , implying always that some precaution has been taken to avert the dreaded contingency, Gen 26:9 for I said, Lest I die on account of her (to obviate which, Isaac had called Rebecca his sister), 31:31 ; 38:11 ; 42:4 ; Exod 13:17 ; Num 16:34 ; 1Sam 13:19 ; 27:11 ( לֵאמֹר ), Psa 38:17 ; with אמר כי implied Gen 26:7 ; compare, with an aposiop., 3:22 and now, lest he put forth his hand, etc. (implying that measures are taken to prevent this, see 3:23 ): compare Tob 8:9. b. מֶּןֿ at the beginning of a sentence, with a dissuasive force, (Beware) lest: + Isa 36:18 חזקיהו אֶתְכֶם מֶּןיַֿסִּית (beware) lest Hezekiah deceive you, Deut 29:17 (twice in verse) (followed by יֵשׁ ), Jer 51:46 ; Job 32:13 ; 36:18 . 2 with Perfect , the result feared being conceived as having possibly already taken place; 2Sam 20:6 pursue after him, וְהִצִּיל ֗֗֗ לוֺ מֶּןמָֿצָא lest he have found him fenced cities, etc. (but the tense of והציל makes יִמְצָא probably, Dr sm Bu Kö iii. 486 ), 2Kin 2:16 י רוּחַ ׳מֶּןנְֿשָׂאוֺ וגו ׳וַיַּשְׁלִכֵהוּ .","rootNote":"from 6437 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 10 4","keyReferences":["1Chr 10 4","1Sam 4 9","1Sam 9 5","1Sam 13 19","1Sam 15 6","1Sam 20 3","1Sam 27 11","1Sam 31 4"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":133,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 10 4","book":"1Chr","chapter":10,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"פֶּן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC"},{"reference":"1Sam 4 9","book":"1S